# BitCapital Research Pool: structural note for February 2026

## Period overview

This document is a revised version of the brief report on BitCapital Research Pool management for February 2026. It is presented in the format of a research-oriented note, where the result is considered together with the state of the environment, loading parameters, distribution logic, and limits of interpretation.

February 2026 unfolded under continued consolidation. The prior downward trend was treated as already broken, while an upward trend was still absent, indicating the continuation of work in an environment without sustained directional movement.

## Market context

The market state during the period was described as consolidating. This meant that the pool management strategy remained oriented not toward operating within a clear trend impulse, but toward using the internal structure of the range while preserving control over total loading.

Under such conditions, capital allocation limits across assets became especially important, as did maintaining a configuration in which the system would remain manageable even without a confirmed upward regime.

## Position management parameters

During the observed period, the following loading structure was permitted:

| Asset | Allowable loading |
|---|---:|
| BTC | up to 25% |
| SOL | up to 36% |
| KEFEN | up to 20% |
| **Total loading** | **no more than 80%** |

Compared with the earlier phase of management, this indicates a somewhat higher allowable total loading while preserving limits on concentration within individual assets. This structure may be interpreted as an attempt to extract a stronger result from a consolidating environment without moving to full pool exposure.

